---
// ============================================================
// terms.astro - Terms & Conditions of Sale (B2B equipment sales)
// Rewritten 2026-09-14: the previous version was a consumer IPTV-service
// document (subscriptions, auto-renewal, account sharing, 7-day refunds) which
// has nothing to do with selling headend equipment. Variable commercial terms
// (payment schedule, Incoterm, warranty period, lead time) are deliberately
// referenced to the order confirmation instead of being invented here.
// ============================================================
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const SITE = 'https://www.iptv-demo.example.com';

const termsSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Terms and Conditions of Sale - FMUSER',
  url: `${SITE}/terms/`,
  description:
    'Terms and conditions of sale for FMUSER digital TV headend equipment: quotations, orders, payment, delivery, inspection, warranty, returns and governing law.',
};

const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Terms of Sale', url: '/terms/' }];
---

<Layout
  title="Terms and Conditions of Sale | FMUSER"
  description="Terms and conditions of sale for FMUSER equipment: quotations, order confirmation, payment, delivery and Incoterms, inspection, warranty, returns and disputes."
  schema={termsSchema}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <section class="py-14 lg:py-20 bg-white" aria-label="Terms and conditions of sale">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4">
      <div class="policy-content">
        <h1>Terms and Conditions of Sale</h1>
        <p><time datetime="2026-09-14">Last updated: September 14, 2026</time></p>
        <p>
          These terms apply to quotations for, and the sale and supply of, equipment and software licences by
          FMUSER ("we", "us", "our"), Guangzhou, China, to a business customer ("you", "buyer"). Where an order
          confirmation or a signed contract states different terms, that document prevails over this page.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Quotations</h2>
        <p>
          Quotations are prepared for the configuration and quantity described in them and are valid for the period
          stated on the quotation. Model numbers, options and lead times are quoted against the datasheet current at
          the time of the quotation; we tell you in writing if a datasheet changes before shipment.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Orders and order confirmation</h2>
        <p>
          An order becomes binding when we issue a written order confirmation (or proforma invoice) and you accept
          it. The order confirmation states the models, quantities, unit prices, currency, payment schedule,
          Incoterms and the delivery window; it is the reference document for the shipment.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Prices, taxes and payment</h2>
        <p>
          Prices are stated in the currency of the quotation and, unless stated otherwise, do not include import
          duties, taxes or charges levied in the destination country. The payment schedule is the one in the order
          confirmation. Unless agreed otherwise in writing, bank charges outside China are for the buyer's account.
          We may suspend production or shipment while an invoice is overdue.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Delivery, Incoterms and risk</h2>
        <p>
          The Incoterms&reg; 2020 rule and the named place or port are stated in the order confirmation. Lead time is
          counted from receipt of the agreed payment and confirmation of the technical details. Risk in the goods
          passes as provided by that Incoterm. Where you ask us to arrange carriage, we do so as your agent and the
          contract of carriage is between you and the carrier.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Inspection, shortages and transit damage</h2>
        <p>
          Inspect the shipment as soon as it arrives and before installation. Report any shortage or visible transit
          damage to us in writing as soon as it is discovered, with photographs of the packaging and the equipment,
          and with the carrier's damage report where one was raised. Claims for damage that occurred in transit are
          pursued against the carrier, and we assist with the documentation.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Warranty</h2>
        <p>
          Equipment is warranted against manufacturing defects for the period stated in the order confirmation,
          counted from delivery. The warranty covers repair or replacement of the defective unit or its faulty
          parts, at our option. It does not cover transit damage, incorrect installation or power supply, misuse,
          unauthorised repair, modification or firmware, consumables and wear parts, or damage from lightning,
          humidity, water or other events outside our control. Warranty service requires the order number and the
          unit serial number.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Returns, DOA and RMA</h2>
        <p>
          Do not return equipment without a return authorisation. Contact us with the order number, serial number,
          a description of the fault and photographs or a short video; we reply with an RMA number and the return or
          replacement instructions. Dead-on-arrival units are handled under the same procedure as warranty claims.
          See <a href="/warranty-returns/">Warranty and Returns</a> for the step-by-step process.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Custom, OEM and ODM orders</h2>
        <p>
          For custom branding, modified specifications, software configuration or custom packaging, the approved
          specification sheet or artwork is the reference for production. Minimum quantities, tooling or
          certification costs and lead time are stated in the quotation for that build. Approved custom builds
          cannot be cancelled once production has started.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Title</h2>
        <p>
          Title to the equipment passes to the buyer on payment in full, or earlier if the applicable law provides
          that title passes on delivery. Until title passes, the buyer holds the equipment as bailee and identifies
          it as our property.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Force majeure</h2>
        <p>
          Neither party is liable for delay or failure caused by events outside its reasonable control, including
          natural events, epidemics, war, civil disruption, strikes, transport or customs interruptions, shortages
          of components, and acts of government. The affected party notifies the other and the delivery window is
          extended accordingly.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          All product designs, firmware, documentation and trademarks remain our property or that of our licensors.
          Datasheets and manuals may be used to evaluate, specify and operate the equipment you buy. They may not be
          republished as your own material or attributed to another manufacturer.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          Our liability for a claim relating to an order is limited to the value of the equipment supplied under
          that order. We are not liable for loss of profit, loss of broadcasting time or audience, loss of data, or
          indirect or consequential loss. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China. The parties first try to settle
          any dispute through discussion between the responsible managers; if that does not resolve it, the dispute
          is submitted to the competent court in Guangzhou, China.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms; the version published here at the time of your order, together with the order
          confirmation, applies to that order. The date at the top of this page shows when it was last revised.
        </p>

        <h2>15. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms, or about a specific order: <a href="mailto:sales@fmuser.com">sales@fmuser.com</a>.
          For technical and configuration questions, use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> so the model details
          are attached to the enquiry.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
